A||N||3||86SEFIERO||power door locks||||1||
Z||000000||86SEFIERO||05-29-2000||04:53 AM||||<BR>my power door locks in my 86 se wont lock my doors the slide moves just a little when I press the button but doesn't lock my doors. How can I fix?||||reg||1
Z||000001||beachbomb||05-29-2000||09:41 AM||||Take your inside door panels off, and spray WD-40 on the elbows and door latch mechanisms. Be careful not to spray the electric door lock actuator. I have an '84 Indy fiero just do this to me, and locks work like a champ now!||||reg||12
Z||000002||Monkeyman||05-29-2000||12:40 PM||||Tap the button a few times.  Does it keep moving the lock?  If so, lube everything.  WD-40 is OK, but a better solution is some spray on lithium grease.  Lasts longer.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ed||05-29-2000||01:20 PM||||Suggest you read archived posts on this subject.  There are a couple of "tricks" which will make your job easier. <P>"The voice of experience"||||reg||1
